3.10 The Stall Holder shall be free from paying the monthly rental during the month July, while only half is required to be paid on the months of June and December;
3.11 In the event the space is ABANDONED for a period of two (2) successive months by the STALL HOLDER, prior to the expiration of this contract without justifiable cause/notice, the LNU-IGO shall have the right to enter the leased premise and to re-let the same and collect the rentals corresponding to the unexpired period of the lease;
3.12 The Stall Holder may withdraw from the contract anytime provided proper FIFTEEN (15) DAY notice shall be given to the LNU-IGO and only upon payment of the rental for the unexpired portion of the lease contract;
3.13 The LNU-IGO may unilaterally terminate the contract and inform the Stall Holders at least thirty (30) days prior in the event of necessary infrastructure development in the area. The two months deposit shall be refunded in full;
3.14 The Stall Holder shall not install, affix or construct permanent fixtures in to their respective spaces. In cases where improvement or modification is necessary to maintain the brand or insignia of the product, they may secure the consent of the LNU-IGO Management. PROVIDED, installation and construction will be shouldered by the Stall Holder without affecting the monthly rental. PROVIDED ALSO, upon termination/end of the contract, the Stall Holder shall restore the leased premise to its original state;
3.15 That the STALL HOLDER shall maintain cleanliness of the leased premise and its vicinity and secure the necessary Permits and Licenses, and Food Handlers Certificate from the City Health Office and/or from the other appropriate agencies. Failure to secure the necessary permits and licenses within the period of one (1) month from the commencement of the contract will result to a four-week temporary closure. If and when, the Stall Holder failed to comply thereafter, it will be the basis for the termination of the lease contract. Permits and licenses shall be displayed in a conspicuous part of the leased premise for public information and shall be available for inspection by health and other regulatory personnel (P.D. 856, Chapter IV, Sec 3.7);
3.15. a That the STALL HOLDER shall be responsible for sanitation and waste disposal, shall undertake necessary remedial measures of potable water supply and distribution system located in the campus, and shall institute appropriate preventive measures to combat the development and spread of communicable diseases on campus;
3.15. b That the STALL HOLDER and Food Handlers shall observe proper sanitary preparation in serving of foods and beverages, and there shall be proper refrigeration of foods and beverages;
3.15. c That the Food Handlers must maintain a high degree of personal cleanliness and must conform to good hygienic practices during all work periods. They must have clean outer garments and wear hair nets;
3.15. d That the Stall Holder must provide a list of the names of food handlers and/or workers and shall pay an equivalent amount for each stall holder and employee to have their IDs issued;
3.15. e That only the Stall Holder and two employees are permitted on the leased property and each should have a health card;
3.16 The LNU-IGO has the obligation to make necessary repairs, like repairs of the sink, functional water system, and repairs to the damaged wall due to termite infestation and rat hole. In the event the LNU-IGO fails to make the necessary repairs within a reasonable time, the STALL HOLDER may withhold payment of rental. However, the STALL HOLDER may opt to undertake such repairs and apply the rentals due, to cover the cost thereof. PROVIDED , that an approved consent of the LNU-IGO Management has been secured. The cost of repairs should be supported with official receipts;
3.17 The leased premises shall be for the personal and exclusive use of the Stall Holder, and shall in no way be sub-leased or allowed to any other person, including the Stall Holder’s relatives and friends;
3.18 That the STALL HOLDER shall make a deposit equivalent to two (2) months rental to the University Cashier within five (5) calendar days after the execution of the contract. The deposit will be used to defray the cost of whatever repair is needed on the stall at the end of the contract. If the repair costs for the damages exceed the two (2) months deposit, the Stall Holder should pay the excess amount. Refusal to pay will disqualify them for future bidding activities;
3.19 The Stall Holder agrees and binds himself and his/her worker (s) to exercise proper courtesy in dealing with the customer or the public;
3.20 In case of food poisoning or sickness or injuries caused by or arising from food intake or consumption of the products/availment of services offered by the STALL HOLDER at the leased premises, the findings of the LNU-IGO or any other appropriate agency, shall be binding to the STALL HOLDER and, on which the basis, the LNU-IGO shall hold the STALL HOLDER liable thereof. The STALL HOLDER shall be solely responsible for, and hold the LNU-IGO free and blameless from any and all administrative, civil and/or criminal liability that may arise therefrom or any other damage in connection to the operation and maintenance of the leased premises;
3.21 The Stall Holder shall abide by the existing rules/policies/regulations including exclusively agreements of the LNU-IGO or that the latter may issue during the effectivity of the contract; and
3.22 The Stall Holder shall faithfully comply with the terms and conditions of the contract. Violation of any provision of this contract will be ground for termination.
3.23 Any record, which may contain personal information, shall be handled in accordance with R.A. 10173 or the Data Privacy Act of 2012.
3.24 Any request for information shall be governed by E.O. No. 2, series of 2016 or the Freedom of Information Policy

