3.5.1 Very Serious Offenses will mean immediate EXCLUSION from the university. The following are considered very serious offenses:
3.5.1.1 Stealing or influencing others to steal;
3.5.1.2 Acts of misbehavior involving destruction of school property or that of the members of the school community, including those guests and visitors;
3.5.1.3 Having somebody else take exams for the student concerned;
3.5.1.4 Illegal possession of deadly weapons;
3.5.1.5 Acts of subversion or insurgency;
3.5.1.6 Instigating, inciting, provoking, leading or taking part in illegal and/or violent demonstrations or activities;
3.5.1.7 Giving support thereto in any manner, whether financial, physical or material to subversive activities;
3.5.1.8 Use or trafficking of prohibited drugs;
3.5.1.9 Observable affiliation in an organization classified as subversive by the government;
3.5.1.10 Inflicting harm and violence against a teacher, a school authority, any personnel or a fellow student in and out of the campus;
3.5.1.11 Misappropriation or failure to account for funds belonging to teh school or to any recognized organization regardless of the amount;
3.5.1.12 Unauthorized use of the name of the Leyte Normal University;
3.5.1.13 Airing complaints directly over the radio, print media and social media without first exhausting proper channels in the University;
3.5.1.14 Offenses against the inviolability of school records, official papers, documents and clearances. These include:
3.5.1.14.1 Destroying, tampering, falsifying school records and official documents;
3.5.1.14.2 Forging signatures of faculty, staff, organization officers and school officials in official documents including clearances; and
3.5.1.14.3 Knowingly using said tampered and falsified documents.
3.5.1.15 Participation in hazing activities;
3.5.1.16 Sexually harassing another student, faculty, or any member of the university community;
3.5.1.17 Display, distribution, and watching of pornographic materials within the University;
3.5.1.18 Misrepresentation;
3.5.1.19 Destroying school facilities, equipment, and other properties;
3.5.1.20 Schoolyard and cyberbullying;
3.5.1.21 Use of school facilities for illegal activities;
3.5.1.22 Such other acts as may herein be determined from time to time by the Student Disciplinary Committee.
3.6 The Preliminary Hearing Committee (PHC) is responsible for assessing the complaint for serious or very serious offense/s committed by students and to determine if it/they warrant a formal investigation.
3.7 The PHC shall be composed of the VPSD, the Supreme Student Council (SSC) Adviser, the Guidance Counselor, and the SSC President.
3.8 The Student Disciplinary Committee (SDC) conducts the formal investigation.
3.9 The SDC shall be composed of the Dean of the student respondent, VPSD, SSC President, and the security guard/faculty/personnel who filed the complaint. In case the complainant is another student, the dean of the complainant sits as the fifth member.

